// s64-R8 (2026-11-13) — Page Crop nomacs parity + wrong-cut fix
// ============================================================
// Root cause: R2 rotateDelta==0 raw-dict write (EngineMupdf.cpp + EngineMupdf_Preview.cpp)
// dropped crop origin (wrote [0 0 cropW cropH]) and never y-flipped fitz y-down cropBox
// to PDF y-up mediabox -> cut region != drawn box (zero-origin bug).
// Fix: real PDF-space rect in BOTH paths:
//   pdfX0 = mb.x0 + cropBox.x0
//   pdfY0 = mb.y1 − cropBox.y1   (y flip: fitz y-down -> PDF y-up, origin preserved)
//   pdfX1 = mb.x0 + cropBox.x1
//   pdfY1 = mb.y1 − cropBox.y0
// Verified: mediabox 100,200,312,492 for fitz box [100,100,412,592]; cut == drawn box exactly.
// Canvas.cpp paint (~:4863-4890): nomacs-parity overlay via Theme API:
//   4 darkened strips outside region (ThemeWindowBackgroundColor alpha 150)
//   + 2px ThemeEdgeColor border + 8 handles (ThemeWindowTextColor alpha 230).
// Coordinate-space lesson: fitz cropBox is y-down page space; PDF mediabox is y-up.
// Never zero origin; always apply y_pdf = mb.y1 − cropBox.y1. Name space of BOTH
// operands before any hit-test (local/root/client/page). Mixed = bug.
